+              <t indent="0" pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-23">ACE4_READ_ATTRIBUTES</t>
+              <ul bare="false" empty="true" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24">
+                <li pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1">
+                  <dl newline="true" spacing="normal" indent="3" pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1.1">
+                    <dt pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1.1.1">Operation(s) affected:</dt>
+                    <dd pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1.1.2">
+                      <t indent="0" pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1.1.2.1">GETATTR of file system object attributes</t>
+                      <t indent="0" pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1.1.2.2">VERIFY</t>
+                      <t indent="0" pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1.1.2.3">NVERIFY</t>
+                      <t indent="0" pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1.1.2.4">READDIR</t>
+                    </dd>
+                    <dt pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1.1.3">Discussion:</dt>
+                    <dd pn="section-6.2.1.3.1-24.1.1.4">The ability to read basic attributes (non-ACLs) of a file.
+On a UNIX system, basic attributes can be thought of as the
+stat-level attributes.  Allowing this access mask bit would
+mean the entity can execute &quot;ls -l&quot; and stat.  If a READDIR
+operation requests attributes, this mask must be allowed for
+the READDIR to succeed.</dd>
